  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_043 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) at 0.725 acc. We have strong evidence that multiprofile + transformer aggregation + scvi_n200 are critical, and that weighted ≈ concat for fusion. However, the image encoder dimension is essentially unexplored in the multiprofile multimodal regime—we have only tested imagenet_vit_l. Image-only performance is very weak (0.227), yet the image modality adds ~7 points over RNA-only in the multimodal setting, so the specific image architecture may matter. Question: config_018 changes only the image encoder from imagenet_vit_l to resnet50 while holding all other settings at their best-performing values (scvi_n200, transformer, weighted, multiprofile). This isolates the effect of image encoder architecture. Why this is the best next experiment: It is a clean single-variable comparison against the current best, it probes the least-understood design axis (image encoder choice in the multiprofile setting), and the result will tell us whether the ViT-specific features are important or whether a standard CNN backbone is sufficient—information that is critical for both further model search and practical deployment, and that cannot be inferred from any existing experiment."
}

